# Build context hygiene. The image only ever needs server/, apps/pricing-hub/
# and apps/menu/scripts/anthonys-seed.json (see server/Dockerfile), but the
# context defaults to the whole repo (~1.4 GB, 40k files). Two of those files
# are actively dangerous if they reach the builder:
#
#   server/node_modules - `COPY server/ .` runs AFTER the builder stage installs
#     Linux modules, so a local (e.g. Windows) tree would overwrite them and the
#     container would fail at runtime.
#   server/.env - runtime secrets belong in env_file on the host, never in an
#     image layer.
#
# Patterns are anchored with a leading slash where they must not match at depth:
# a bare `pricing-hub` would also exclude apps/pricing-hub and break the build.

# --- never ship local dependencies or secrets ---
**/node_modules
server/.env
server/.env.*
server/data
*.log
/direct-run.log

# --- repo scaffolding and knowledge base the runtime never reads ---
/.git
/.github
/brain
/docs
/invoices
/nrs
/supabase
/pricing-hub
/assets
/BOD-1.mp4

# --- apps/ is ~980 MB; only pricing-hub + the menu seed are copied ---
apps/delivery
apps/inventory
apps/superkitchen
